title: Quantum (as in Schrodinger's cat) information can overcome the dictator problem.
pid: dacd1b57-e2d9-4015-9d88-b103fc410031
body: |2-
  A loud minority of humans avoid and resent Wikipedia for dictating a single truth around a given topic. Whether that criticism is fair can be debated, but the criticism cannot apply to Skg.

  In Skg there is room for all knowledge, multiply categorized. Different writers can testify to different things. Nobody dictates "the" article on anything; there are only views onto the collective information. You curate what you see, can promote and render invisible (to yourself and anyone who wants your fork) whole people or person-topic pairs, however you wish. The result will be comprehensible and navigable, due to two innovations: (1) graphs, and (2) letting the user, not an alien invisible algorithm, choose what to see.
